NAME
       sudoers - rules for sudo

DESCRIPTION
       /etc/sudoers is read by sudo(8). Supported subset of the usual
       grammar:

       Comments start with # (but #include, #includedir and #uid are not
       comments). A trailing backslash continues the line.

       @include FILE, @includedir DIR (also #include, #includedir). In a
       directory, names containing a dot or ending in ~ are skipped.

       Aliases: User_Alias, Runas_Alias, Host_Alias, Cmnd_Alias, written
       NAME = item, item : NAME2 = item.

       User specification:
              who host = (runas_user[:runas_group]) [NOPASSWD:|PASSWD:] cmd, cmd
       who is a user, %group, #uid, an alias, ALL, with ! for negation. host
       is ALL, a host name or an alias. cmd is an absolute path, a path with
       arguments, a directory ending in /, ALL or an alias. The last
       matching rule wins.

       Defaults [!cmd | >runas | :user | @host]: secure_path, env_keep (=,
       +=, -=), env_reset, timestamp_timeout, passwd_tries, targetpw,
       rootpw. insults and lecture are accepted and ignored; other unknown
       options are reported by visudo and ignored by sudo.

FILES
       /etc/sudoers, /etc/sudoers.d/

SEE ALSO
       sudo(8), visudo(8)
